[00:00.14] The boy woke up again today from a terrible nightmare.
[00:05.56] The bad memories of the past that he wanted to forget reappeared in his dreams every night, continuing to torment him.
[00:15.20] Terrified of falling asleep, the boy eventually went to a witch and pleaded:
[00:21.74] "Witch, please, erase all the bad memories in my head so that I never have to dream a nightmare again.
[00:29.24] Then, I will give you whatever you want."
[00:33.56] Years passed and the boy became an adult; he no longer had nightmares, but for some reason,
[00:40.14] he was not the least bit happier.
[00:43.26] On a night when a red full moon rose,
[00:47.38] the witch finally reappeared before him to collect the price for his wish. He shouted in a voice full of resentment:
[00:56.86] "All my bad memories were erased, so why?
[01:00.54] Why haven't I become happy?"
[01:09.04] “아프고
[01:10.24] 고통스러웠던 기억,
[01:11.56] 처절하게 후회했던 기억, 남을 상처 주고 또 상처받았던 기억,
[01:17.54] 버림받고 돌아섰던 기억.
[01:20.20] 그런 기억들을 가슴 한구석에 품고 살아가는 자만이 더 강해지고,
[01:25.66] 뜨거워지고,
[01:27.22] 더 유연해질 수가 있지.
[01:30.76] 행복은 바로 그런 자만이 쟁취하는 거야.
[01:35.16] 그러니 잊지 마.
[01:37.00] 잊지 말고 이겨내.
[01:39.04] 이겨내지 못하면 너는 영혼이 자라지 않는 어린애일
[01:45.72] 뿐이야.”
